  "body": "Issue #4: the saved profile points toward nested admission-receipt checking as the larger archive-reader cost, ahead of worker-row and grid checks. [Full result, tables and terminal commands](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/f078d2a/docs/archive-reader-edges.md#historical-result--november-17).\n\nThe seven defining functions were fixed in the [prospective plan](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/issues/4#issuecomment-6957605618). Source `b26374f` was public before extraction. The query reuses unchanged graph authentication and direct-edge calculation, checks producer hashes/AST coordinates, preserves all 2,354 frames/5,640 edges and every selected incoming/outgoing edge, and requires child/self conservation within the fixed absolute 1e-7 seconds. Missing, ambiguous or recursive selected frames and changed inputs reject.\n\nHistorical `read_saved` inclusive elapsed is 125.551543 seconds. Its direct admission-check edge is 107.961533 and direct prerequisite-load edge is 17.361320. Prerequisites serve two direct reader calls and twelve receipt-profile-check calls. Nested totals overlap and include waits/profiling overhead; shared grandchildren are not assigned to a single caller. This identifies a next measurement target, not current CPU or savings.\n\nBoth actual data readers reproduce all five numerical exports byte-for-byte after source publication, with 104 construction/profiling targets blocked, zero forbidden calls and all 15 raw producer files unchanged. The committed Git blobs match those exports exactly. The binary is hashed only; no new profiler, solver or poker trajectory runs. [Data receipts and hashes](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/f078d2a/results/archive-reader-edges/data-checks/manifest.json).\n\n**Final qualification passed at `f078d2a922ef395c5f617562eba379ab605717b3`:**\n\n- Local bases: 5,434 passed / 70 skipped / 150 deselected each (772.20/741.54 seconds), including strict typing825, lint, formatting and hooks.\n- Optional suites: 2,342 each (488.81/423.50 seconds).\n- [Hosted CI](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/actions/runs/44154403223): 5,434 each, one existing warning (1329.88/1125.82 seconds).\n- Actual Python3.11.17/NumPy2.4.6 and Python3.12.15/NumPy2.5.4, all hosted uv selections, clean source before/after, all455 source hashes and equality of the entire tested checkout tree verified. Corrected local roles run without extra `PYTHONPATH`.\n\nThe initial source and report CI jobs failed test collection because the new test imported scripts before setting its path; the local launcher had masked this with extra `PYTHONPATH`. Test-only `f078d2a` fixes its own imports. [Failed report-head jobs and interrupted local checks](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/f078d2a/results/archive-reader-edges/failed-qualification-b5/manifest.json) are retained; initial source-head logs are also retained for the closing archive. None counts as final success. All455 scientific bytes and numerical results remain unchanged. All54 focused cases also pass with a reference-loaded parent and a fresh guarded child.\n\nThis PR includes PR87's [39 closing records](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/f078d2a/results/earlier-source-profile/final-ci/manifest.json), journal132 and work-log updates. Self-review: defining aliases, shared callers, complete identities/edges, raw preservation and fresh-child test isolation checked. Next measure current nested receipt/context CPU inside the complete unchanged reader before proposing reuse. No cache, algorithm/dependency/CI/seed/cap/gate change. Runtime912.54/900 and accuracy2.390%/1% stay failed; no strength/default/global admission. Codex-assisted implementation, checks and drafting; no independent human review, personal practice or hours inferred.",
